INT. SHUTTERED ROLLER RINK - NIGHT

Disco ball dark. Rental skates hang in rows on the wall. A buffet of foil trays sits on the skate counter, untouched.

ROSALIND ABARA (40s, black dress, shoes in her hand) stands at the edge of the rink floor. CASPIAN ABARA (40s, rumpled suit) sits on the bench lacing a pair of rental skates. PERPETUA (70s, church hat) watches from a plastic chair. HAKON (30s, borrowed tie) stands very straight by the jukebox. JUNE (20s, ripped tights) leans on the counter, scrolling. OLU (10) crouches beside the skate rack, counting wheels.

She sets the shoes down. He doesn't look up.

ROSALIND
You're not serious.

CASPIAN
He wanted music.

ROSALIND
He wanted a hymn.

He finishes the knot. Stands. Wobbles. Nobody helps.

PERPETUA
Let him.

Hakon feeds a coin into the jukebox. It coughs. A faint organ riff leaks out. June looks up from her phone. Olu stops counting.

JUNE
That's not a hymn.

HAKON
It was on his list.

She crosses to the jukebox and reads the label. Her jaw sets. She walks back and takes the phone from June's hand, locks it, and puts it in her own pocket.

JUNE
Hey.

ROSALIND
Not tonight.

He rolls out onto the floor, arms out, one wheel dragging. The sound fills the hall. Olu hurries over and holds the rail. Perpetua grips the arm of her chair. Hakon turns the volume up.

CASPIAN
(over the music)
Come on.

ROSALIND
No.

CASPIAN
Come on.

She stares at the floor, at the scuffed centre circle. Then she steps onto it in stocking feet. He takes her hand. They go round once, awkward, slow. Behind them Perpetua stands. June finally laughs, one sharp note, and covers her mouth.
